   Oh, my God. You're right.

427
00:19:35,542 --> 00:19:37,341
         I do do that.

428
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:38,976
      Honey, I'm so sorry.

429
00:19:38,978 --> 00:19:42,880
That's okay.
Just... kiss my neck.

430
00:19:45,117 --> 00:19:47,518
        (rumbling stops)
         It's working!

431
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,788
 I just remembered I also used
      to blow in your ear!

432
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:53,524
          (blows air)
    Oh, Stan.

433
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:56,961
That really turns me on.
          (blows air)

434
00:19:56,963 --> 00:19:59,864
   Francine, why didn't you tell
     me you were so unsatisfied?

435
00:19:59,866 --> 00:20:01,232
    I don't know!

436
00:20:01,234 --> 00:20:03,834
I guess I was afraid
of hurting your feelings.

437
00:20:03,836 --> 00:20:05,670
Now lick my neck

438
00:20:05,672 --> 00:20:09,407
and tell me I'm your favorite
horse in the stable!

439
00:20:09,409 --> 00:20:12,176
        You're my favorite horse
          on the whole frontier.

440
00:20:12,178 --> 00:20:14,011
   (neighs, pants)

441
00:20:14,013 --> 00:20:15,846
Now talk like you're
the Monopoly guy!

442
00:20:15,848 --> 00:20:18,249
         (à la Thurston Howell):
                  Oh, you freak.
              You lovable freak.

443
00:20:18,251 --> 00:20:19,984
                    Keep telling
                  me what to do.

444
00:20:19,986 --> 00:20:23,654
I didn't say Thurston Howell!
I said the Monopoly guy!

445
00:20:23,656 --> 00:20:25,856
        (kissing sounds)
       (Francine screams)

446
00:20:25,858 --> 00:20:29,493
      (Francine yodeling)

447
00:20:29,495 --> 00:20:31,762
          (bell rings)

448
00:20:34,266 --> 00:20:36,601
           MAURICIO:
          I'm a-free!

449
00:20:38,437 --> 00:20:41,739
    Bull's-eye.
         (door creaks)

450
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:46,244
    This house... is clean.

451
00:20:46,246 --> 00:20:48,546
   But as for those sheets...

452
00:20:48,548 --> 00:20:51,282
   babadababadababadababada-

453
00:20:51,284 --> 00:20:54,385
                   babadababada-
                   babadababada-

454
00:20:54,387 --> 00:20:57,622
   <i>babadababadababadababada...</i>

455
00:21:02,861 --> 00:21:05,896
  Oh, Klaus, I heard you were
       in Atlantic City.

456
00:21:05,898 --> 00:21:08,699
          Did you try
 that new restaurant Roppongi?

457
00:21:08,701 --> 00:21:10,101
I didn't go there
to eat.

458
00:21:10,103 --> 00:21:11,969
I went there
to improve myself.

459
00:21:11,971 --> 00:21:13,404
Which I did do.

460
00:21:13,406 --> 00:21:14,739
          Oh, yeah? In what way?

461
00:21:14,741 --> 00:21:16,207
I'm just better,
okay?!

462
00:21:16,209 --> 00:21:18,442
               Klaus, chill out.
        We're all happy for you.

463
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:20,111
Well, it doesn't sound
like that.

464
00:21:20,113 --> 00:21:22,413
Geez, you guys need to be more
like a government bond...

465
00:21:22,415 --> 00:21:24,215
and mature.
                 (chuckles)

466
00:21:24,217 --> 00:21:25,950
     Klaus, that's pretty funny.
     Did you just think of that?

467
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:29,887
I've been thinking
about it for a few days.

468
